 "equipment_type": "Power meter (circuit breaker trip unit)",
 "applies_to": "ABB SACE PR122/P and PR123/P (Emax) and PR332/P and PR333/P (Emax X1, Tmax T7, Tmax T8) protection releases with the Modbus RTU communication module, per 1SDH000556R0001.",
 "summary": "ABB's PR12x and PR33x electronic trip units talk Modbus RTU through the PR120/D-M (or PR330/D-M) com module. Run-time measures (currents, voltages, power, energy, frequency) and breaker state are input registers; commands such as open, close and trip reset go to two holding registers. 32-bit values are sent low word first.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 247,
  "baud": 19200,
  "parity": "Even",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "The map gives relative addresses with 30001 (input registers, function 4) and 40001 (holding registers) bases; its example says run-time measures at offset 200 are 30201, relative address 200. The relative address is what goes on the wire with the default 'Standard' addressing type."
 },
 "default_word_order": "CDAB",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "Modbus system Interface for Protection relays PR122/P and PR123/P + communication module PR120/D-M, mounted on CB New Emax; Protection relays PR332/P and PR333/P + communication module PR330/D-M, mounted on CB Emax X1, Tmax T7 and Tmax T8",
  "doc_number": "1SDH000556R0001",
  "revision_date": null,
  "url": "https://library.e.abb.com/public/89aa30f1720540cfaf50e2e1da987829/1SDH000556R0001.pdf",
  "pages": "Comms parameters p. 6; Modbus map and word order p. 11; register map p. 14; commands p. 17; statistics p. 18; state pp. 20-22; run-time measures pp. 23-24; information p. 24; command conditions p. 42; configuration p. 25"
 },
 "notes": [
  "The document states 4-byte values are sent with the low-order word at the lower address (LOW-HIGH), bytes within a word high first, so 32-bit registers here are CDAB.",
  "'Not available' is shown as 2^32-1 (unsigned currents), 2^31-1 (signed power) or 2^16-1 (voltages, frequency).",
  "Input register 102 bit 5 shows whether the measuring module is present; the protection table says it is always fitted on PR122/PR332 LSIRc and on PR123/P and PR333/P. Ground current registers apply to G versions.",
  "The com module can be set to 'ABB' addressing (register 1029); this map assumes the factory 'Standard' addressing.",
  "Left out: per-phase reactive/apparent power, peak factors, harmonics (600+), trip/measure history, logger, waveform and parameter areas.",
  "State 1 (100) bits are 'glitch' bits that clear on read; state 3, 5, 6, 7 and 9 words are not transcribed.",
  "Commands are accepted only while the unit is in Remote mode, and with a test unit connected only CB Open is accepted (commands execution conditions, p. 42)."
 ],
